{
  "_comment": [
    "The trustd service definition, and the trust store's own keys.",
    "",
    "Identity is LocalService. trustd needs no privilege at all: it reads a",
    "file the ca-certificates package ships, reads the registry, and writes",
    "/system/retc/ssl. Nothing it holds is secret -- the root set is public,",
    "which is also why its socket is open to everyone. Private keys are",
    "deliberately not trustd's: a key holder is a signing oracle under",
    "compromise and wants the opposite security posture, so machine identity",
    "belongs to a future key service, not here.",
    "",
    "(peinit today materialises every non-SYSTEM identity as a SYSTEM token",
    "carrying the service SID -- PEI-329. The intent is recorded here so",
    "that when service logon exists nothing about trustd has to change.)",
    "",
    "Readiness is Notify (0): trustd sends READY=1 once it has composed the",
    "store and rendered it. Anything that speaks TLS should carry",
    "Requires = [\"trustd\"], because on a live image /system/retc is empty",
    "every boot and an unrendered store means no trust at all.",
    "",
    "RestartPolicy is Always (2). A machine whose trust store is stale is",
    "one that cannot learn a certificate was revoked.",
    "",
    "The Trust keys are created here, empty, so that trustd's watch has a",
    "target the moment it starts and an operator can find the knobs. The",
    "roots themselves are NOT here: they are package data, because reg apply",
    "is additive and Mozilla's removals would otherwise linger for ever.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the trustd package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an",
    "image names it in [registry] autoapply."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Services" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\trustd",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath", "type": "sz", "data": "/usr/sbin/trustd" },
        { "name": "Triggers", "type": "multi", "data": ["boot"] },
        { "name": "Identity", "type": "sz", "data": "LocalService" },
        { "name": "Readiness", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "RuntimeDirectories", "type": "multi", "data": ["trustd"] },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy", "type": "dword", "data": 2 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "DisplayName", "type": "sz", "data": "Trust store" },
        { "name": "Description", "type": "sz", "data": "Composes the machine's CA trust from the shipped roots and the registry, and serves it" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Trust",
      "values": [
        { "name": "GenerateLinuxTrustFiles", "type": "dword", "data": 1 }
      ]
    },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Trust\\Certificates" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Trust\\Certificates\\Add" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Trust\\Certificates\\Distrust" }
  ]
}
